  "id": "Compound::DB00229 - Gene::9356",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Cefotiam may interact with Slc22a6 through a shared mechanism involving cephalosporin antibiotics. Multiple paths indicate that Cefotiam, Cefpiramide, and Ceftriaxone, all members of the cephalosporin class, bind to Slc22a6. This is supported by the fact that these compounds are all similar to one another and share a common ancestor in the cephalosporin family. The low scores in the paths suggest that the similarity between the compounds is a key factor in their interaction with Slc22a6. The recurring evidence points to a potential role of Slc22a6 in transporting or regulating the uptake of these cephalosporins, possibly through a common mechanism that involves the same transport protein. The integration of these paths highlights the importance of the cephalosporin class in mediating the interaction between Cefotiam and Slc22a6, emphasizing the role of this protein in drug transport and potentially in drug resistance.",
